WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.753
A fund holds investments.

2
00:00:01.873 --> 00:00:07.469
An exchange-traded fund, or ETF, holds a collection of assets and trades on an exchange.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.463
Spread concentration.

4
00:00:09.583 --> 00:00:13.844
Holding different investments can reduce dependence on one company’s result.

5
00:00:14.375 --> 00:00:15.873
Look inside the basket.

6
00:00:15.993 --> 00:00:18.605
Two funds may own many of the same companies.

7
00:00:18.725 --> 00:00:21.326
More tickers do not always mean more variety.

8
00:00:21.846 --> 00:00:23.193
Risk still remains.

9
00:00:23.313 --> 00:00:25.751
A broad stock fund can fall with the market.

10
00:00:25.871 --> 00:00:28.622
Funds also have fees and different strategies.

11
00:00:29.142 --> 00:00:30.582
Compare before choosing.

12
00:00:30.702 --> 00:00:33.906
Study a fund’s holdings, costs, and purpose.

13
00:00:34.026 --> 00:00:37.370
Practice comparing stocks and ETFs in Sprout.

